                'title' => 'Delete from a BST',
                'problem' => [
                    'title' => 'Delete from a BST',
                    'description' => 'Insert the n values one by one, in the order given, into an empty binary search tree, delete the node with value x, and print the preorder traversal of the tree that is left: the root, then the left subtree in preorder, then the right subtree in preorder.

To insert a value, start at the root. Go left if the value is smaller than the current node and right if it is larger, until there is no node in that direction, and put the new node there. Never rebalance the tree.

Delete x by these rules:
- No children: remove the node.
- One child: replace the node with its child.
- Two children: find the smallest value in its right subtree (the successor), copy that value into the node, then remove the successor node from the right subtree. The successor has no left child, so one of the first two rules removes it.

Input
Line 1: n, the number of values.
Line 2: the n values in insertion order, separated by single spaces.
Line 3: x, the value to delete.

Output
One line with the preorder values, separated by single spaces (an empty line when the tree is empty).

Constraints
1 <= n <= 1000
-1000000 <= each value <= 1000000
All values are distinct.
x is a value in the tree.',
