                    'title' => 'Running median',
                    'description' => 'Read the n numbers in order. After each one, print the median of all the numbers read so far.

For an odd count, the median is the middle number once they are sorted. For an even count, it is the average of the two middle numbers: print it as a whole number if it is whole, and otherwise with exactly one decimal, .5 (for example -2.5, 3 or 7.5).

Input
Line 1: n, the number of numbers.
Line 2: the n numbers, separated by single spaces.

Output
n lines: line i holds the median of the first i numbers.

Constraints
1 <= n <= 2000
-2147483648 <= each number <= 2147483647 (any 32-bit signed integer)',
